Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

terrio adapts code and data from the projects below. The copyright in that code and data remains
with its authors, whose notices follow. The licenses of the Rust crates terrio's packages and
binaries are built with are in LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY.md.

terrio follows the REUSE specification (https://reuse.software). Each source file derived from
another project's source files starts with SPDX headers: the copyright lines of those source
files, copied verbatim, the licenses that apply, and the files it was translated or adapted from.
Files written to match another program's behavior, without translating its code, say so in a
comment. The REUSE.toml of the terrio repository (https://github.com/opengeos/terrio) records the
copyright and license of the other files, and its LICENSES/ directory holds the license texts.
The sections below gather, project by project, the derived files, the copyright
notices of their sources and the license terms.

