Independent implementations
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The deferred linework MakeValid implementation and its helpers formerly in
crates/terrio/src/tiles/valid.rs have been removed. The replacement in
crates/terrio/src/tiles/repair/ was independently implemented against a behavioral
specification and executable reference observations, under a documented isolated
process. It is part of Terrio's MIT-licensed code, not part of the JTS ports above.
See docs/make-valid-implementation.md for task-local provenance, validation and
limitations. This record makes no repository-wide licensing certification.

SOZip specification

The independent implementation in crates/terrio/src/vsi/sozip.rs follows version 0.5.0
of the SOZip specification by Even Rouault (2023):
https://github.com/sozip/sozip-spec/blob/master/sozip_specification.md
The specification is licensed under CC BY 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Its license notice explicitly excludes source and binary code derived from the
specification from the scope of its copyrighted material.
The independent chunk decoding step adapts Annex F under its offered CC0-1.0 option.

The original Rust SQLite page/overflow layout and pointer-map implementations in
crates/terrio/src/drivers/sqlite_edit.rs and sqlite_repack.rs follow SQLite's file-format
documentation: https://www.sqlite.org/fileformat2.html

